{
  "an7.22:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 7.22 ",
  "an7.22:0.2": "3. The Vajji Seven ",
  "an7.22:0.3": "With Vassakāra ",
  "an7.22:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "an7.22:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha, on the Vulture’s Peak Mountain. ",
  "an7.22:1.3": "Now at that time King Ajātasattu of Magadha, son of the princess of Videha, wanted to invade the Vajjis. ",
  "an7.22:1.4": "He said: ",
  "an7.22:1.5": "“I shall wipe out these Vajjis, so mighty and powerful! I shall destroy them, and lay ruin and devastation upon them!” ",
  "an7.22:2.1": "And then King Ajātasattu addressed Vassakāra the brahmin, a chief minister of Magadha, ",
  "an7.22:2.2": "“Please, brahmin, go to the Buddha, and in my name bow with your head to his feet. Ask him if he is healthy and well, nimble, strong, and living comfortably. ",
  "an7.22:2.3": "",
  "an7.22:2.4": "And then say: ",
  "an7.22:2.5": "‘Sir, King Ajātasattu of Magadha, son of the princess of Videha, wants to invade the Vajjis. ",
  "an7.22:2.6": "He said: ",
  "an7.22:2.7": "“I shall wipe out these Vajjis, so mighty and powerful! I shall destroy them, and lay ruin and devastation upon them!”’ ",
  "an7.22:2.8": "Remember well how the Buddha answers and tell it to me. ",
  "an7.22:2.9": "For Realized Ones say nothing that is not so.” ",
  "an7.22:3.1": "“Yes, worthy sir,” Vassakāra replied. He went to the Buddha and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "an7.22:3.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sa